  "created": "2026-08-10T15:32:23.457Z",
  "description": "Turns a product's licensing files into compile-checked code. One `*.product.json` goes in and the feature and limit keys come out as consts plus the declaration the runtime needs — so a mistyped feature key is a compiler error instead of a capability that is silently off, and the same file is the descriptor the licence registry imports. One `*.keyring.json` exported by the issuing service goes in and the trusted public keys come out as a `const string`, which is the shape string encryption can defend — an embedded resource is a blob anyone can swap for their own key without touching an instruction.",
